Organizing directory nested inside a described archive, exercising the case satx-shape-and-purpose v0.0.8 calls most likely to be got wrong: the boundary sits inside described territory rather than outside it. Holds this language's interface message catalogs, gettext .po files: no sidecar, no work, no Dublin Core. Split by what is being translated, bin/ and lib/, matching the split at the instance root. English needs no catalog of its own here, since it is the source language the CLI's strings are written in; both subdirectories are correctly empty. Per SAT Sidecars: Config and Metadata v0.0.13, a catalog lives in the archive of the language it translates to, not under lib/locale/; only the language-neutral .pot templates live there.
